      ":question/id": "60c1b44f-848f-5486-a155-69e3743b20fe",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-214693",
      ":question/problem": "Find the solution to the inequality $2<x+5<7.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$x\\,<$\n{{field-3}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition principle, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & <x+5<7 \\\\ 2-5 & <x+5-5<7-5 \\\\ -3 & <x<2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-3<x<2.$"
